  "[{\"subclass_definition\": \"Refractivity is a Radiation Reflectivity that inheres in a bearer in virtue of the capacity of that bearer to change the direction of a propagating wave when passing through the bearer.\", \"subclass_iri\": \"https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000826\", \"superclass_definition\": \"Optical Property is a Disposition to Interact with Electromagnetic Radiation that inheres in a bearer in virtue of being realized when the bearer interacts with electromagnetic waves within the visible light spectrum.\", \"superclass_iri\": \"https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000784\"}]": [
    {
      "gemini_plausibility": 1.0,
      "gemini_rationale": "The normalized definition of Refractivity explicitly states it is a type of 'Radiation Reflectivity', and the superclass 'Optical Property' is defined as a 'Disposition to Interact with Electromagnetic Radiation'. Since radiation reflectivity is a disposition to interact with electromagnetic radiation, and changing the direction of a propagating wave when passing through is a specific interaction with radiation, the subclass relationship is strongly supported."
    }
  ],
